            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Innovations</strong><br>\nLiszt's contributions to the concept of the recital and the symphony orchestra were revolutionary. He is also credited with developing the technique of thematic transformation, a form of musical metamorphosis.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nLiszt passed away on July 31, 1886, leaving behind a vast body of work, including piano compositions, orchestral works, and church music. His innovations laid the groundwork for future developments in music.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Influence and Memory</strong><br>\nLiszt's influence extends beyond his compositions. His thinking and performance style transformed the way piano music was conceived, making him a towering figure in the history of Western music. His legacy continues to inspire musicians and listeners alike.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
